%S A401883 0,0,1,3,5,7,15,41,97,195,383,817,1833,4019,8503,17889,38273,82771,
%T A401883 178287,381137,813625,1742739,3741575,8027233,17194641,36818483,
%U A401883 78891775,169128465,362533001,776848435,1664514519,3566951393,7644586273,16383311763,35109124367
%N A401883 Coefficient of sqrt(6) in x(n), where x(1) = 1, x(2) = 2 and x(n) = x(n-1) + sqrt(6)*x(n-2).
%C A401883 x(n) = A401882(n) + a(n)*sqrt(6) is the apothem of the central regular tetrahedron at level n of an additive pyramidal fractal, measured in units of the apothem of the seed tetrahedron; see A401882 for the construction.
%C A401883 a(n) collects the contributions that pass through an odd number of factors sqrt(6) (projections of heights at 30 degrees).
%C A401883 A401882(n)/a(n) tends to sqrt(6).
%H A401883 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (2,-1,0,6).
%F A401883 a(n) = a(n-1) + A401882(n-2), where A401882(n) = A401882(n-1) + 6*a(n-2).
%F A401883 a(n) = 2*a(n-1) - a(n-2) + 6*a(n-4) for n >= 5.
%F A401883 G.f.: x^3*(1 + x)/(1 - 2*x + x^2 - 6*x^4).
%e A401883 x(4) = x(3) + sqrt(6)*x(2) = (2 + sqrt(6)) + 2*sqrt(6) = 2 + 3*sqrt(6), so a(4) = 3.
%t A401883 LinearRecurrence[{2, -1, 0, 6}, {0, 0, 1, 3}, 40]
%o A401883 (Python)
%o A401883 def a(n):
%o A401883     r, s = [1, 2], [0, 0]
%o A401883     for k in range(2, n):
%o A401883         r.append(r[k-1] + 6*s[k-2]); s.append(s[k-1] + r[k-2])
%o A401883     return s[n-1]
%Y A401883 Cf. A010464, A041006, A401882.
%K A401883 nonn,easy,new
%O A401883 1,4
%A A401883 _Juan Antonio Piña Malacara_, Nov 08 2026
